# Lesson `# description` (under `# title`)

The **`# description`** block is **catalog / LMS-facing copy**. Write it as **plain explanatory prose** (complete sentences, natural voice). **Do not** compress it into **README-style “text-only”** blurbs.

## Avoid

- Opening like **“Bài gồm phần … và phần …”** / **“This lesson includes … and …”** as the main skeleton (reads like a readme TOC).
- A **single dense sentence** stuffed with stack keywords in parentheses (**NestJS**, **OpenTelemetry**, …) instead of weaving them into readable sentences.
- Bullet-like enumeration disguised as one line (**phần thực hành … phần lý thuyết …**) without narrative flow.

## Prefer

- **Two to four short sentences**: problem or situation → what the learner does → what ideas they leave with.
- Name tools (**NestJS**, **OpenTelemetry**, **Jaeger**, …) **inside prose**, only where they clarify what the learner runs or installs—not as a naked toolchain list.

Keep **`vi.md`** and **`en.md`** descriptions **aligned in meaning** (not literal word-for-word translation unless natural).
